  "pack": "NY-US",
  "about": "Which threshold rows apply to which matrix and parameter, in which unit, with which analytical method. Read by scripts/validate_input.py and scripts/demo.py; rendered to core/screening-matrix.md by scripts/render_matrix.py. Values, legal status and dates live only in the packs (core/thresholds/*.json): this file holds row IDs, never numbers. A matrix with 'series' is a medium that varies by season: one sampling event there is flagged with the closing sample. Covers Module 1 (PFAS) and well nitrate for the New York / US federal pack; other modules and the EU pack are not mapped yet.",
  "fit_legend": {
    "object": "the row applies to the object directly (default)",
    "farmland": "a reference written for farmland or rural soil; sets the summary status of a group of fields",
    "other land use": "a reference written for another land use (e.g. remedial-site soil guidance); sets the status of the individual field, is printed beside the group summary, and does not set the group summary (references/status-rules.md §3a)"
  },
